mpler/backend, precision, reward parsing, group schedule, held-out evaluation, and decontamination can all change the result. fileciteturn0file0 The attached paper also says the controlled audit should hold the full Min-Report-RL block identical across arms except the variant’s defining delta; Table 2 lists DAPO’s defining delta as “clip-higher + dyn. sampling.” fileciteturn1file4\\n\\nThe key registry rule is:\\n\\n> **Every registry entry must contain a `defining_delta` and at least one `report` whose `min_report_rl` object has all seven required fields. Unknown values are allowed, but only as explicit `unknown` / `not_reported` fields, never by omission.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. JSON Schema\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema\\\",\\n  \\\"$id\\\": \\\"https://grpo-registry.org/schemas/gvr-entry-v0.1.0.schema.json\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"GRPO-family Variant Registry Entry\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n  \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n  \\\"required\\\": [\\n    \\\"schema_version\\\",\\n    \\\"registry_id\\\",\\n    \\\"variant\\\",\\n    \\\"defining_delta\\\",\\n    \\\"reports\\\",\\n    \\\"governance\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"properties\\\": {\\n    \\\"schema_version\\\": {\\n      \\\"const\\\": \\\"gvr.entry.v0.1.0\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"registry_id\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n      \\\"pattern\\\": \\\"^gvr:[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_.-]*$\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"variant\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n      \\\"additionalProperties\\\": false,\\n      \\\"required\\\": [\\n        \\\"canonical_name\\\",\\n        \\\"family\\\",\\n        \\\"base_algorithm\\\",\\n        \\\"aliases\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"properties\\\": {\\n        \\\"canonical_name\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n        },\\n        \\\"family\\\": {\\n          \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n          \\\"examples\\\": [\\\"GRPO-family\\\"]\\n        },\\n        \\\