 -lc nl -ba /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.tex | sed -n '489,529p'\",\"ct\":1777864926.939832},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc pdfinfo /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.pdf | sed -n '1,80p'; echo '--- text page 1 ---'; pdftotext -f 1 -l 1 -layout /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.pdf - | sed -n '1,120p'\",\"ct\":1777864929.587958},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc kpsewhich llncs.cls || echo 'no llncs'; which pdflatex || true\",\"ct\":1777864936.353718},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc command -v pdflatex || echo no-pdflatex; ls /mnt/data | grep -i llncs || true\",\"ct\":1777864939.600691},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"titles = [\\n\\\"Auditing Advantage Collapse in GRPO Fine-Tuning with Zero-Variance Fraction\\\",\\n\\\"Auditing Zero-Variance Fraction for Advantage Collapse in GRPO\\\",\\n\\\"Zero-Variance Fraction in GRPO: Diagnostic, Not Predictor\\\",\\n\\\"Zero-Variance Fraction for Auditing GRPO in RLVR Fine-Tuning\\\",\\n\\\"Stratified Audits of Zero-Variance Fraction in GRPO\\\",\\n\\\"Task-Stratified Evaluation of Zero-Variance Fraction in GRPO\\\",\\n\\\"Zero-Variance Fraction Reveals Task Confounding in GRPO Diagnostics\\\",\\n\\\"Advantage-Collapse Diagnostics for GRPO Under Task Stratification\\\",\\n\\\"Auditing GRPO Advantage Collapse Across Tasks, Group Sizes, and Backends\\\",\\n\\\"GRPO Diagnostics Across Qwen3 Models, Tasks, and Backends\\\",\\n]\\ncurrent=\\\"Zero-Variance Fraction in GRPO: A Stratified Audit of Advantage-Collapse Diagnostics\\\"\\nimport re\\nfor t in [current]+titles:\\n    words = len(t.replace(\\\":\\\",\\\"\\\").replace(\\\",\\\",\\\"\\\").split())\\n    print(words, len(t), t)\\n\",\"ct\":1777864942.714976},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"Budget basis: current title is **10 words / 84 characters**. Every option below is **6–8 words and shorter than the current title**, so the concrete edit is: **replace only `\\\\title{...}` on lines 37–38; delete nothing from the body; do not touch the author block; add no figures.**\\n\\n| Rank | Alternative title | Words | Rationale | Page-budget action |\\n|---:|---|---:|---|---|\\n| 1 | **Zero-Variance Fraction for Auditing Advantage Collapse in GRPO** | 8 | Best balance of novelty, method, failure mode, and GRPO discoverability. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 2 | **Auditing GRPO Advantage Collapse with Zero-Variance Fraction** | 7 | Stronger verb-led framing; makes the paper sound like an empirical audit rather than a metric-only paper. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 3 | **Stratified Zero-Variance Diagnostics for GRPO Fine-Tuning** | 6 | Signals the key statistical caution: ZVF must be interpreted under stratification, not pooled blindly. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 4 | **Zero-Variance Fraction in Verifiable-Reward GRPO Fine-Tuning** | 6 | Good for RLVR readers because it names the reward setting and fine-tuning context. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 5 | **Group-Size Sensitivity and Zero-Variance Diagnostics in GRPO** | 7 | Captures the practical contribution around \\\\(G \\\\in \\\\{2,4,8,16\\\\}\\\\) and ZVF diagnostics. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 6 | **Diagnosing GRPO Collapse Across Group Sizes and Backends** | 8 | Highlights the broader empirical study across \\\\(G\\\\), Tinker, Modal/veRL, and TRL. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 7 | **A Stratified Audit of Zero-Variance Fraction in GRPO** | 8 | Closest to the current title but cleaner and less abstract than “advantage-collapse diagnostics.” | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 8 | **Zero-Variance Fraction Under Stratification in GRPO Fine-Tuning** | 7 | Focuses on the pooled-versus-within-task correlation result, but underplays group-size ablation. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 9 | **When GRPO Loses Advantage Signal: A Zero-Variance Audit** | 8 | More memorable and accurate for the all-wrong/all-correct collapse regimes, but slightly less formal. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n| 10 | **Critic-Free GRPO Diagnostics for Verifiable-Reward Fine-Tuning** | 6 | Relevant to the RL-fine-tuning audience, but weaker because it hides the paper’s named metric. | Replace lines 37–38 only; shorter than current title. |\\n\\n**Recommendation:** use **“Zero-Variance Fraction for Auditing Advantage Collapse in GRPO.”** It is the strongest title for an RL-fine-tuning audience because it front-loads the paper’s named contribution, keeps **GRPO** searchable, and includes the concrete failure mode, **advantage collapse**. I would leave `\\\\titlerunning{Zero-Variance Fraction in GRPO}` unchanged, since it remains accurate and short.\",\"ct\":1777865213.031511}]},{\"id\":\"69f81091-4f30-83e8-a35d-ff3c9e425171\",\"title\":\"Paper Revision Suggestions\",\"create_time\":1777864850.791382,\"update_time\":1777865458.178982,\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"slug\":null,\"t\":\"Both files attached: Conference_paper_springer.pdf (12-page rendered LNCS) and .tex (819-line source, inline thebibliography{25} at line 690, monolithic file).\\n\\nHARD CONSTRAINTS — apply to every suggestion:\\n- 12-page LNCS limit, currently at exactly 12pp. Every addition must be matched by a deletion. Be specific.\\n- Author block (8 authors, all PES University, Arvind C R + Sandhya Jeyaraj co-first) must stay byte-identical to NeurIPS variant — do not touch.\\n- No figures (LNCS variant is text-only by design).\\n\\nLimitations and overclaiming audit. Read Section 7 (Discussion and Conclusion, lines 578–684) carefully. Quote every phrase that overclaims relative to the experimental scope (single base-model family, single benchmark per claim, no human eval, no reasoning-trace analysis). For each, propose a softening that preserves the contribution's punch without inviting reviewer rejection. Then propose 3 honest limitations that should be added but currently aren't, with line numbers showing where to insert them. Page-neutral via deletions you specify.\",\"ct\":1777864849.172},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc cat /home/oai/skills/pdfs/SKILL.md\",\"ct\":1777864854.053507},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"I’ll audit Section 7 in the TeX source for exact line-numbered overclaims, using the PDF only to check page neutrality. Every proposed addition will be matched with concrete deletions, without touching the author block or adding figures.\",\"ct\":1777864864.441806},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc ls -R /home/oai/skills | sed -n '1,120p'\",\"ct\":1777864867.990215},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc find / -maxdepth 4 -type f -name SKILL.md 2>/dev/null | head -50\",\"ct\":1777864874.014112},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc nl -ba /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.tex | sed -n '540,720p'\",\"ct\":1777864877.506737},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc nl -ba /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.tex | sed -n '1,180p'\",\"ct\":1777864882.665024},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc nl -ba /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.tex | sed -n '300,578p'\",\"ct\":1777864886.140099},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc nl -ba /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.tex | sed -n '180,300p'\",\"ct\":1777864889.689138},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc pdfinfo /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.pdf 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,80p' && echo '---' && pdftotext -layout /mnt/data/Conference_paper_springer.pdf - | sed -n '1,60p'\",\"ct\":1777864893.993109},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"sl