eric failure of GRPO at\\nscale, and a hyperparameter sweep at $14$B is left for future work.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport re\\ndef count(s):\\n    words = re.findall(r\\\"[A-Za-z0-9\\\\\\\\$=\\\\{\\\\}~\\\\._:-]+\\\", s)\\n    return len(words), len(s)\\ncount(orig)\\n\",\"ct\":1777864939.587956},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"rewrite = r\\\"\\\"\\\"The Qwen3-14B Tinker GRPO row in Table~\\\\ref{tab:main_results}\\n(last-10 $=0.437$, peak $=0.750$) is the table's largest single-row\\nanomaly, below both the Qwen3-8B base ($0.820$) and Qwen3-4B Tinker\\nGRPO ($0.850$ last-10). Its trace is consistent with, but does not\\nestablish, collapse in this seed: ZVF exceeds $0.6$ within $10$ steps,\\nentropy falls to a near-deterministic mode, and reward-stability crosses\\n$0.6$ at step~$15$, matching the failed $G{=}2$ signature in\\nSection~\\\\ref{sec:results}. Alternative explanations remain possible:\\n14B-specific defaults, data order or prompt mix, backend/hardware effects,\\nand RNG. We therefore report this as a configuration-level negative result:\\nthe tested Tinker default did not transfer naively to 14B; a matched,\\nmulti-seed 14B sweep is needed to establish mechanism.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\ncount(rewrite)\\n\",\"ct\":1777864975.949199},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"rewrite2 = r\\\"\\\"\\\"The Qwen3-14B Tinker GRPO row in Table~\\\\ref{tab:main_results}\\n(last-10 $=0.437$, peak $=0.750$) is the largest single-row anomaly,\\nbelow the Qwen3-8B base ($0.820$) and Qwen3-4B Tinker GRPO ($0.850$\\nlast-10). Its trace is consistent with, but does not establish, collapse\\nin this seed: ZVF exceeds $0.6$ within $10$ steps, entropy falls to a\\nnear-deterministic mode, and reward-stability crosses $0.6$ at step~$15$,\\nmatching the failed $G{=}2$ signature in Section~\\\\ref{sec:results}.\\nAlternative explanations remain possible: 14B-specific defaults, data\\norder or prompt mix, backend/hardware effects, and RNG. We therefore\