nls /mnt/data/neurips_v5/renders/zvf | head && cat /tmp/render_zvf.log | tail -5\",\"ct\":1777305737.967533},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc find /mnt/data/neurips_v5/renders -maxdepth 2 -type f | head -20; tail -20 /tmp/render_zvf.log /tmp/render_dnb.log /tmp/render_workshop.log 2>/dev/null\",\"ct\":1777305780.31602},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc find /mnt/data/neurips_v5/renders -maxdepth 2 -type f | wc -l && ls /mnt/data/neurips_v5/renders/zvf | tail\",\"ct\":1777305783.765361},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"import math\\ndef fisher_ci(r,n,alpha=0.05):\\n    z=math.atanh(r)\\n    se=1/math.sqrt(n-3)\\n    zcrit=1.959963984540054\\n    lo=math.tanh(z-zcrit*se)\\n    hi=math.tanh(z+zcrit*se)\\n    t=r*math.sqrt((n-2)/(1-r*r))\\n    # two-sided p using scipy?\\n    return lo,hi,t\\nfor r,n in [(0.4,19),(0.13,7),(-0.21,33),(-0.769,15)]:\\n    print(r,n,fisher_ci(r,n))\\n\",\"ct\":1777305827.420695},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc grep -RInE \\\"US-East|non-OECD|anonymous/|wandb|huggingface\\\\.co/anonymous|HuggingFace|regional|country|author|unpaid|institutional|Thinking Machines|Modal|Tinker SDK|student|domestic|same region|collaborator|JWT|W&B|anonymous\\\\.4open|Do not distribute|Submitted to|academic research group\\\" /mnt/data/neurips_v5/*.txt | head -200\",\"ct\":1777305837.0041},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc ls /mnt/data/neurips_v5\",\"ct\":1777305872.736694},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc ls -la /mnt/data | head -50\",\"ct\":1777305876.019635},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc mkdir -p /mnt/data/neurips_v5 && unzip -q /mnt/data/neurips_review_v5.zip -d /mnt/data/neurips_v5 && for f in /mnt/data/neurips_v5/*.pdf; do pdftotext -layout \\\"$f\\\" \\\"${f%.pdf}.txt\\\"; done && grep -RInE \\\"US-East|non-OECD|anonymous/|wandb|huggingface\\\\.co/anonymous|HuggingFace|regional|country|author|unpaid|institutional|Thinking Machines|Modal|Tinker SDK|student|domestic|same region|collaborator|JWT|W&B|anonymous\\\\.4open|Do not distribute|Submitted to|academic research group|Address|email\\\" /mnt/data/neurips_v5/*.txt | head -250\",\"ct\":1777305879.841534},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc grep -RInE \\\"https?://[^ ]+\\\" /mnt/data/neurips_v5/*.txt | sed -n '1,200p'\",\"ct\":1777305885.311092},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc sed -n '1045,1105p' /mnt/data/neurips_v5/main_dnb.txt; sed -n '1180,1200p' /mnt/data/neurips_v5/main_dnb.txt\",\"ct\":1777305889.97758},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc grep -RIn \\\"wandb.ai\\\\|huggingface.co/anonymous\\\\|anonymous/tinker\\\" /mnt/data/neurips_v5/*.txt\",\"ct\":1777305893.262391},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"I’ve confirmed ZVF is more conservative now, but still framed like a benchmark; the main remaining lever is recasting it as a negative-result audit with a useful sentinel.\",\"ct\":1777305893.552335},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"First: fix desk-risk items before adding experiments. The current PDFs still say “39th Conference” while the official 2026 call says the **Fortieth** NeurIPS; use the 2026 style/footer, keep main content to **9 pages**, and ensure all linked artifacts are anonymized because NeurIPS applies double-blind policy to linked code/material too. citeturn792918view0turn562047view0\\n\\n## A. ZVF main-track: highest-probability path\\n\\n**Current ceiling without new training:** ~22-27%.  \\n**Ceiling with all recommended analyses + open-stack multi-seed replication + held-out eval:** ~32-38%, optimistic max ~40%.  \\n**No single move is sufficient.** The path is to make it a focused statistical-audit paper, not a benchmark paper.\\n\\n### A1. Required move list\\n\\n| Move | Add/change/run | Impact | Cost | Status |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\\n| **Retitle/reframe** | Replace current “A Unified Benchmark…” title. Lead with “ZVF is a per-step zero-gradient sentinel, not a cross-task predictor.” Move benchmark breadth to artifact appendix. | +4-6 pp | 3-5 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Drop/move drift-proxy section** | Move current reward-instability/KL-proxy Fig. 1 to appendix or DNB. It distracts and is not the ZVF claim. | +3-5 pp | 3-5 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Bootstrap/permutation table** | Add 95% CIs + permutation p-values for pooled N=15/N=33, GSM8K N=19, model-varying N=7. | +2-3 pp | 2-4 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Partial-correlation / residualized audit** | Add task-FE, task+G, task+baseline/early-accuracy partial correlations; residualized scatter. | +4-6 pp | 6-10 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Positive sentinel figure** | Replace current Fig. 2 with a tool-use sentinel case study: ZVF=1, GU=0, reward=0 from step 1; add triage table. | +4-6 pp | 6-10 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Held-out eval for available GSM8K checkpoints** | Evaluate saved adapters/checkpoints on held-out GSM8K; report train-reward vs held-out scatter. | +4-8 pp | 8-16 h + 5-30 GPU-h | **High-leverage** |\\n| **Open-stack multi-seed mini-grid** | Run TRL/OpenRLHF/veRL or TRL-only controlled GSM8K grid: Qwen3-8B, G={4,8,32}, 3 seeds, full ZVF telemetry + held-out eval. | +6-10 pp | 135-270 H100-h for 9 runs; ~$530-$1,067 on Modal H100 | **Needed to exceed ~30%** |\\n| **Open-stack tool-use sentinel replication** | 3-5 seeds on cheap open model/tool-use reward; show ZVF sentinel is not Tinker-only. | +3-5 pp | 15-40 GPU-h | **Efficient marginal** |\\n| **Single-cell G=8 3-seed replication** | Qwen3-8B/GSM8K/G=8 only. | +1-2 pp | 45-90 H100-h; ~$178-$356 on Modal H100 | **Marginal; not enough** |\\n| **Step-level existing-data analysis** | Mixed/run-FE or block-bootstrap regression: Δreward\\\\_{t+1:t+5} ~ GU\\\\_t + reward\\\\_t + step. | +2-4 pp | 6-12 h | **Useful marginal** |\\n\\nModal’s current H100 price page lists H100 at $0.001097/sec, about $3.95/GPU-h, so a 15-30 H100-h seed is roughly $59-$119. citeturn840474search1\\n\\n### Title\\n\\nYes, retitle. Do **not** use the current benchmark title.\\n\\nBest high-probability title:\\n\\n**Zero-Variance Fraction in GRPO: A Stratified Audit of Advantage-Collapse Diagnostics**\\n\\nAcceptable sharper version:\\n\\n**When Zero-Variance Fraction Misleads: A Stratified Audit of GRPO Reward-Collapse Diagnostics**\\n\\nI prefer the first. “Misleads” is memorable but slightly overclaims; “Stratified Audit” is safer and reviewer-proof.\\n\\n### Strongest positive companion claim\\n\\nUse this exact framing:\\n\\n> ZVF is not a cross-task predictor of GRPO performance. It is a per-step sentinel for zero reward-gradient contribution under group-relative advantages. When ZVF\\\\_t=1, every rollout group in the batch has zero reward variance, so the reward-driven GRPO advantage is zero for every sampled completion. GU\\\\_t=1−ZVF\\\\_t is therefore an online utilization meter. Pairing ZVF with batch reward mean distinguishes all-wrong collapse from all-correct saturation.\\n\\nAdd one main figure:\\n\\n**Figure 2: ZVF as a zero-gradient sentinel.**\\n\\nPanels:\\n\\n1. **Tool-use ZVF trace:** Qwen3-32B/tool-use and Llama-3.1-8B/tool-use, ZVF=1 from step 1 through end.\\n2. **Tool-use reward trace:** reward remains 0; GU=0.\\n3. **GSM8K contrast:** a GSM8K run with nonzero GU and nonzero reward movement.\\n4. **Triage table:** columns: run, task, steps, mean ZVF, mean GU, first step triggering ZVF≥0.99, last-10 reward, interpretation.\\n\\nAdd one small table:\\n\\n| Regime | ZVF | Reward mean | Interpretation | Action |\\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\\n| All-wrong collapse | ~1 | ~0 | zero reward-gradient; task/reward too hard | redesign reward/curriculum |\\n| All-correct saturation | ~1 | ~1 | zero reward-gradient; task solved | stop or increase difficulty |\\n| Useful contrast | <1 | intermediate | informative groups exist | continue training |\\n| Cross-task pooled signal | mixed | mixed | confounded by task identity | do not rank runs |\\n\\nThis is the most defensible positive result.\\n\\n### Multi-seed replication: do not spend the budget on only G=8\\n\\nA 3-seed Qwen3-8B/GSM8K/G=8 replication is **not** enough to materially improve the within-GSM8K Pearson r. It estimates variance for one cell; it does not create enough independent configuration-level variation to repair the correlation analysis.\\n\\nBetter:\\n\\n**Run G={4,8,32} × 3 seeds** on one open stack, ideally TRL or OpenRLHF, same model, same data, same token budget, full ZVF telemetry, held-out GSM8K eval.\\n\\nMinimum acceptable if time is tight:\\n\\n**G={4,8,32}, 2 seeds each + reuse existing seed** if exactly comparable.\\n\\n### Bootstrap CIs and permutation p-values\\n\\nYes. Add them.\\n\\nApproximate Fisher CIs to expect:\\n\\n| Analysis | Current r | N | Approx 95% CI | Message |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\\n| Pooled original | -0.769 | 15 | [-0.92, -0.42] | strong but task-confounded |\\n| Pooled larger | -0.21 | 33 | [-0.52, +0.15] | weak/unstable |\\n| GSM8K within-task | +0.40 | 19 | [-0.07, +0.72] | sign flips; underpowered |\\n| GSM8K model-varying | +0.13 | 7 | [-0.64, +0.66] | no detectable association; very wide |\\n\\nDo not hide the wide N=7 CI. Say: “This is not evidence of absence; it is evidence that the pooled monotone story is not supported once the task confound is removed.”\\n\\n### Partial correlations\\n\\nYes. Add a table titled:\\n\\n**Table: Pooled ZVF-performance correlations collapse under stratification and controls.**\\n\\nRows:\\n\\n1. Raw pooled N=33.\\n2. Task fixed effects.\\n3. GSM8K-only N=19.\\n4. GSM8K model-varying N=7.\\n5. Task + log group size.\\n6. Task + baseline or first-step accuracy.\\n7. Task + group size + baseline/early accuracy.\\n8. Optional: stack fixed effects, but label as underpowered.\\n\\nImportant: do **not** control for final/last-10 reward if last-10 reward is the outcome. Use base accuracy, held-out base accuracy, first-step reward, or pre-RL accuracy.\\n\\n### Other existing-data replications\\n\\nUse these, but label them correctly:\\n\\n| Existing analysis | Use | Impact | Caveat |\\n|---|---|---:|---|\\n| **Within-G=8 across stacks** | Descriptive stack sanity check | +1-2 pp | checkpoint/runtime confounds; not central |\\n| **Step-level ZVF → next reward change** | Run-FE/block-bootstrap prequential analysis | +2-4 pp | avoid pseudo-replication |\\n| **Early-ZVF prediction** | Mean ZVF steps 1-5 vs final/held-out outcome | +2-3 pp | exploratory |\\n| **Advantage-variance identity check** | Show ZVF=1 implies advantage variance=0 in logs | +2-3 pp | supports sentinel claim |\\n| **Held-out checkpoint audit** | Train reward vs held-out GSM8K | +4-8 pp | high value if checkpoints exist |\\n\\n### ZVF final probability\\n\\nIf you do only rewrite + stats + no new training: **~22-27%**.  \\nIf you add only the 3-seed G=8 cell: **~23-28%**.  \\nIf you add held-out eval + open-stack G mini-grid + sentinel replication: **~32-38%**, optimistic ceiling **~40%**.\\n\\nIf the open-stack multi-seed grid cannot finish, ZVF main remains below the ~30% threshold. Then submit ZVF as workshop/TMLR-style empirical audit and let DNB carry the NeurIPS E&D attempt.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## B. DNB E&D: push beyond 35-45%\\n\\nE&D is the better fit. The 2026 E&D call explicitly includes evaluation audits, benchmark/failure-mode analyses, negative results, tools, datasets, and artifacts; it also requires accessible, documented code when the contribution is a reusable artifact. citeturn792918view1\\n\\nTarget after fixes: **~52-62%**.\\n\\n| Move | Add/change/run | Impact | Cost | Status |\\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\\n| **Cut to compliant 9-page main** | Current DNB content appears to spill to page 10. Move full ethics/carbon/manifest to appendix; keep 5-line main limitation. | desk-risk removal | 3-6 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Artifact-first rewrite** | Title/abstract: “reproducible artifact for auditing RL post-training across stacks,” not “frontier benchmark.” | +5-7 pp | 6-10 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Replace giant Table 4 in main** | Move frontier/single-seed table to appendix. Main table = evidence tiers + artifact availability + reproducibility. | +4-6 pp | 4-8 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **One-command reproducibility** | Add `make reproduce-main`, `make smoke-test`, expected runtime, hardware, hash manifest, exact outputs. | +5-8 pp | 12-24 h | **Necessary for E&D** |\\n| **Artifact card / auditability matrix** | For every run: seeds, stack, raw rollouts?, ZVF trace?, checkpoint?, held-out?, tier. | +5-7 pp | 6-12 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Held-out eval expansion** | Evaluate all available GSM8K adapters/checkpoints; show train-reward inflation vs held-out. | +4-7 pp | 8-16 h + inference | **High-leverage** |\\n| **One extra multi-seed open-stack cell** | Best: cheap matched TRL vs OpenRLHF/veRL cell, 3 seeds, same model/data/hparams. Alternative: Qwen3-8B TRL G=8, 3 seeds. | +3-6 pp | 45-90 H100-h or cheaper small-model run | **Marginal but useful** |\\n| **Claims hierarchy rewrite** | Every claim labeled A/B/C in abstract, main table, conclusion. No unsupported universal laws. | +4-6 pp | 4-8 h | **Necessary** |\\n| **Remove hype names** | Replace “Bitter Lesson Campaign,” “World-Class Suite,” “frontier winner” language with neutral case-study labels. | +2-4 pp | 1-2 h | **Necessary polish** |\\n| **Croissant/metadata/model cards** | Add machine-readable dataset/artifact metadata if releasing traces as dataset-like artifact. | +2-4 pp | 4-8 h | **Useful** |\\n\\nBest extra experiment for DNB is **not** another Tinker frontier run. It is a small, clean, open-stack replication that demonstrates the artifact’s reproducibility value.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## C. Workshop: turn weak accept into clear accept\\n\\nCurrent likely range: **60-75%**.  \\nAfter one strong polish pass: **75-85%**.\\n\\nDo this:\\n\\n| Move | Exact change | Impact | Cost |\\n|---|---|---:|---:|\\n| **Make it an artifact note, not a compressed main paper** | First page: artifact card + one-sentence claim hierarchy. Remove broad benchmark ambition. | +5-7 pp | 3-5 h |\\n| **One killer figure** | Combined figure: ZVF heatmap/tool-use sentinel + residualized within-task ZVF scatter. | +5-8 pp | 4-6 h |\\n| **Add tiny statistical ablation** | Bootstrap CI + permutation p-values for pooled vs stratified correlations. Fits in 1/4 page. | +3-5 pp | 2-4 h |\\n| **End with workshop questions** | Keep current discussion prompts; make them sharper and concrete. | +2-3 pp | 1 h |\\n\\nNo new training is required for workshop. The marginal winning move is the **combined figure + CI table**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## D. Anonymity polish\\n\\nMinimum edits:\\n\\n| Residue | Replace with |\\n|---|---|\\n| “Modal H100 (US-East)” | “Commercial H100 provider, region withheld for review” |\\n| “US-East region as configured” | “commercial region withheld for anonymity; US-average carbon factor used as conservative proxy” |\\n| “non-OECD national grids” | “regional grid-intensity range 0.4-0.8 kg CO2e/kWh; exact region withheld” |\\n| “specific city and country withheld” | delete entirely |\\n| “single-institution, single-region context” | “narrow author/infrastructure context” |\\n| “six student-FTE-months, unpaid” | “substantial human engineering time; not monetized” |\\n| “shared access to one A100 node” | “shared institutional GPU resource” |\\n| `https://wandb.ai/anonymous/...` | remove from PDF; expose through 4open/OpenReview supplement only |\\n| `https://huggingface.co/anonymous/...` | remove from PDF; mirror artifacts via 4open/OpenReview supplement |\\n| `anonymous/tinker-rl-bench-*` | “anonymous adapter namespace; details in artifact manifest” |\\n\\nExtra risks I would check:\\n\\n1. PDF hyperlink annotations, not just visible text. Your DNB PDF has actual hyperlink annotations to `wandb.ai/anonymous/tinker-rl-bench` and `huggingface.co/anonymous/tinker-rl-bench-*`; remove the annotations too.\\n2. W&B run metadata: entity, username, run creator, machine hostname, timezone, git commit, code path.\\n3. Hugging Face model cards: owner, commit author, upload timestamps, license contact, hidden README metadata.\\n4. Git history: remotes, author emails, `.git/config`, old commits, branch names.\\n5. Logs/configs: `/home/<user>`, `/Users/<user>`, Modal app names, Tinker org/project IDs, S3/GCS bucket names, JWT/API-key error logs.\\n6. LaTeX build artifacts: `.synctex`, `.fls`, comments in `.tex`, bibliography owner notes.\\n7. The footer/template: fix “39th Conference” to the 2026 template.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## E. Submission strategy\\n\\nNeurIPS explicitly warns that main, E&D, and position tracks have different portals and that papers cannot be submitted to multiple tracks/types simultaneously; duplicate or irrelevant papers risk desk rejection. citeturn792918view0\\n\\nOptimal portfolio:\\n\\n| Paper | Venue | Submit? | Notes |\\n|---|---|---:|---|\\n| **DNB / TinkerRL-Bench** | **NeurIPS E&D** | **Yes, primary** | Best fit and highest expected value. Do not submit DNB to main. |\\n| **ZVF** | **NeurIPS main** | **Yes only if de-overlapped** | Must be a focused statistical-audit paper, not a second benchmark paper. Remove duplicated DNB tables/claims. |\\n| **Workshop variant** | NeurIPS workshop | **Yes, later** | Submit one focused artifact/diagnostic note, subject to workshop policy. NeurIPS lists suggested workshop contribution date Aug. 29 and mandatory decisions Sept. 29. citeturn368402view0 |\\n| **ZVF to E&D** | E&D | **No if DNB goes E&D** | Too much overlap; fold ZVF into DNB as an example diagnostic. |\\n| **DNB to main** | Main | **No** | E&D fit is substantially stronger. |\\n| **Two workshop papers** | Same workshop | Usually no | Combine unless the workshop explicitly allows multiple distinct submissions. |\\n\\nBest high-upside plan:\\n\\n1. Submit **DNB to E&D** as the serious acceptance target.\\n2. Submit **ZVF to main** only after the retitle/rewrite/statistical audit and after removing overlap with DNB.\\n3. Prepare **one workshop version** as the fallback/visibility path, centered on the artifact + ZVF sentinel/confound story.\\n4. Do not let DNB and ZVF share the same title, same main figures, or same primary contribution statement.\",\"ct\":1777306457.781991}]},{\"id\":\"69ef79d1-15bc-83e8-a2bf-219b08dfe00d\",\"title\":\"Pre-Submission Review Updates\",\"create_time\":1777301970.456593,\"update_time\":1777302943.509526,\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"slug\":null,\"t\":\"Final pre-submission sanity pass. You reviewed v3 of these papers earlier today and gave: ZVF main 6.0, E&D 6.5, Workshop 7.5. The author has applied every consistency blocker you flagged in v3. This is round-4 verification, not a fresh review.\\n\\nWhat changed since v3:\\n\\n1. **Run manifest** (sections/run_manifest.tex) reconciled cell-for-cell with main results:\\n   - New \\\"Tier B - Bitter Lesson Campaign\\\" section: 8 single-seed Tinker frontier rows at 30 steps each.\\n   - New \\\"Tier B - Group-Size Ablation\\\" section: explicit single-seed rows per G in {2,4,8,16}.\\n   - ZVF N=7 model-varying GSM8K rows promoted from Tier-C/0-step to Tier-B† with actual step counts (qwen3.5-4b 30, gpt-oss-20b 30, kimi-k2 20, nemotron-120b 20, deepseek-v3.1 20).\\n   - Tier-A \\\"qwen3-8b (G-sweep) N=14, 3 seeds\\\" corrected to \\\"qwen3-8b (Wave-6 ablation) N=12, 1 seed, 30 steps\\\".\\n\\n2. **DNB (main_dnb.pdf, 31pp)**:\\n   - Title tightened to E&D-aligned: \\\"TinkerRL-Bench: A Cross-Stack Artifact for Studying RL Post-Training of Language Models (with Stratified ZVF Diagnostics)\\\".\\n   - Table 4 G=8 row: 100% / 84.4% -> 81.2% / 34.4% (matches Figure 5 / Appendix C / master_results.csv). Added missing G=32 row.\\n   - Added \\\"Stratified within-task analysis (consistency note)\\\" paragraph after pooled correlation: r=+0.40 N=19 GSM8K, r=+0.13 N=7 model-varying.\\n   - Figure caption for zvf-correlation rewritten to flag pooled scatter as task-confounded.\\n   - Training Protocol seed accounting reconciled with manifest.\\n\\n3. **Workshop (main_workshop.pdf, 16pp)**:\\n   - \\\"3B-671B\\\" -> harmonized \\\"0.6B-671B total (0.6B-37B active for largest MoE)\\\".\\n   - Modal H100 -> Modal L4 for Qwen2.5-0.5B row (matches manifest + carbon table).\\n   - Added stratified within-GSM8K result paragraph (r=+0.40, r=+0.13).\\n   - Fixed broken Table ?? cross-reference on page 8.\\n\\n4. **ZVF (main_zvf.pdf, 22pp)**:\\n   - Evidence-grade table: within-task null demoted A -> B (table legend says A = multi-seed/definitional; within-task null is single-seed-per-cell closed-backend).\\n   - Removed \\\"please cite these, not the pooled correlation\\\" advocacy phrasing.\\n   - Title left as is; TODO comment added for author decision on retitle to \\\"When Zero-Variance Fraction Misleads: A Stratified Audit of GRPO Reward-Collapse Diagnostics\\\".\\n\\n5. **Cross-cutting**:\\n   - Appendix A.3 causal overstatement softened: \\\"because the group-relative advantage has collapsed\\\" -> mechanical claim + softer \\\"co-occurrence with reward plateaus\\\".\\n   - GU overload resolved: appendix's token-budget gradient utilization renamed to TBGU with $\\\\widehat{\\\\mathrm{TBGU}}$ symbol throughout group_size_reconcile.tex.\\n   - \\\"G=32\\\" claim removed from both ethics statements: now says \\\"budget-dependent group-size selection\\\".\\n   - Closed-backend boilerplate aligned with headline: primary inferential claims explicitly limited to (i) mechanical theorem + (ii) held-out 5-seed Qwen3-8B GSM8K control; Tinker-derived stratified correlations are artifact analyses with closed-backend caveats.\\n\\nWhat I want from you:\\n\\nA. **Verification, not re-review.** Open each PDF and check: did each of the v3 blockers actually land in v4? List any that did NOT land or that landed but introduced a new inconsistency.\\n\\nB. **Final pre-submission readiness verdict** for each variant:\\n   - **DNB**: ready to submit to NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets as the author's primary, or still needs blocker fixes? If still has blockers, list them precisely.\\n   - **Workshop**: ready to submit to a NeurIPS workshop (target TBD)? If not, what specifically.\\n   - **ZVF main**: any change to your \\\"do not submit to main track\\\" verdict? (Your v3 estimate was 12-18% acceptance probability after polish; updated number?)\\n\\nC. **Anonymity sanity check** (third pass). Quick scan for any deanonymizing residue across all 3 PDFs: institution names, regional grid intensity numbers, gender pronouns, named collaborators, repository slugs that aren't the canonical anonymous.4open.science URL.\\n\\nD. **Updated submission strategy** if anything has changed.\\n\\nBe terse this round. We don't need a full rewritten review — we need confirmation that the v3 blockers are gone, an anonymity sanity check, and a go/no-go per variant. If you find anything that's still broken, be specific (file, page, exact wording).\",\"ct\":1777301968.615},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc cat /home/oai/skills/pdfs/SKILL.md && echo '---ZIP---' && ls -lah /mnt/data && unzip -l /mnt/data/neurips_review_v4.zip | sed -n '1,200p'\",\"ct\":1777301974.56947},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"I’ll treat this as a targeted v4 verification pass, not a fresh review: check the named fixes, scan for anonymity residue or new inconsistencies, then give go/no-go per variant.\",\"ct\":1777301984.947054},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc cat /home/oai/skills/pdfs/tasks/read_review.md\",\"ct\":1777301990.372115},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc rm -rf /mnt/data/v4 && mkdir -p /mnt/data/v4 && unzip -q /mnt/data/neurips_review_v4.zip -d /mnt/data/v4 && for f in /mnt/data/v4/*.pdf