           for i,l in enumerate(page.splitlines(),1):\\n                    if pat in l:\\n                        print('page',pno,'line',i,':',l.strip())\\n                        for j in range(max(0,i-2),min(len(page.splitlines()),i+3)):\\n                            print(' ',page.splitlines()[j].strip())\\n                        print()\\nPY\",\"ct\":1777302340.039359},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc for b in main_dnb main_workshop main_zvf; do echo '###' $b; rg -n \\\"qwen3-8b \\\\(G=32\\\\)|Qwen3-8B \\\\(G=32\\\\)|G=32\\\\)\\\" /mnt/data/v4_text/$b; done\",\"ct\":1777302357.542611},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc for b in main_dnb main_workshop main_zvf; do echo '###' $b; rg -n \\\"qwen3-8b \\\\(G=32\\\\)|Qwen3-8B \\\\(G=32\\\\)|G=32\\\\)\\\" /mnt/data/v4_text/$b.txt || true; done\",\"ct\":1777302363.286945},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc sed -n '1748,1765p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_dnb.txt\",\"ct\":1777302367.035926},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc python - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\npatterns=['G ∈ {2, 4, 8, 16, 32}', 'Qwen3-8B (G=32)', 'Tier B — Group-Size Ablation', 'qwen3-8b (G=16)']\\nfor fname in ['main_dnb','main_workshop','main_zvf']:\\n    text=Path(f'/mnt/data/v4_text/{fname}.txt').read_text(errors='replace')\\n    print('###',fname)\\n    for pno,page in enumerate(text.split('\\\\f'),1):\\n        for pat in patterns:\\n            if pat in page:\\n                for i,l in enumerate(page.splitlines(),1):\\n                    if pat in l:\\n                        print('page',pno,'line',i,':',l.strip())\\nPY\",\"ct\":1777302372.005271},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc sed -n '520,540p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_dnb.txt; sed -n '376,388p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_zvf.txt\",\"ct\":1777302389.365875},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc sed -n '760,820p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_workshop.txt\",\"ct\":1777302392.523456},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc python - <<'PY'\\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nsel = {\\n 'dnb':[('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_dnb/page-06.png','DNB p6'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_dnb/page-07.png','DNB p7'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_dnb/page-09.png','DNB p9'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_dnb/page-14.png','DNB p14'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_dnb/page-26.png','DNB p26'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_dnb/page-30.png','DNB p30')],\\n 'workshop':[('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_workshop/page-02.png','WS p2'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_workshop/page-08.png','WS p8'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_workshop/main_workshop_page15-15.png','WS p15')],\\n 'zvf':[('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_zvf/main_zvf_page7-07.png','ZVF p7'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_zvf/main_zvf_page13-13.png','ZVF p13'),('/mnt/data/v4_renders/main_zvf/main_zvf_page22-22.png','ZVF p22')]\\n}\\nthumbs=[]\\nfor group, items in sel.items():\\n    for path,label in items:\\n        img=Image.open(path).convert('RGB')\\n        img.thumbnail((400,520))\\n        canvas=Image.new('RGB',(420,560),'white')\\n        canvas.paste(img,((420-img.width)//2,30))\\n        d=ImageDraw.Draw(canvas); d.text((10,10),label,fill='black')\\n        thumbs.append(canvas)\\ncols=3; rows=(len(thumbs)+cols-1)//cols\\nsheet=Image.new('RGB',(cols*420, rows*560),'white')\\nfor i,img in enumerate(thumbs):\\n    sheet.paste(img,((i%cols)*420,(i//cols)*560))\\nsheet.save('/mnt/data/v4_contact.png')\\nprint('/mnt/data/v4_contact.png')\\nPY\",\"ct\":1777302409.464148},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc for b in main_dnb main_workshop main_zvf; do echo '###' $b; rg -n -i \\\"TODO|FIXME|author decision|retitle|anonymous author|affiliation|do not distribute|camera-ready|submission|v3|v4|reviewer\\\" /mnt/data/v4_text/$b.txt | head -120; done\",\"ct\":1777302434.047596},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc for b in main_dnb main_workshop main_zvf; do echo '###' $b; rg -n \\\"\\\\b(he|she|his|her|hers)\\\\b\\\" /mnt/data/v4_text/$b.txt | head -50; done\",\"ct\":1777302441.67839},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc sed -n '646,674p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_dnb.txt; sed -n '254,278p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_workshop.txt; sed -n '580,606p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_zvf.txt\",\"ct\":1777302451.363922},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc sed -n '708,720p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_dnb.txt; sed -n '316,325p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_workshop.txt; sed -n '642,651p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_zvf.txt\",\"ct\":1777302458.252415},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc sed -n '250,314p' /mnt/data/v4_text/main_zvf.txt\",\"ct\":1777302469.87441},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"I’ve found one likely residual DNB consistency issue: stale “Qwen3-8B G-sweep” seed/cell wording conflicts with the corrected Wave-6 manifest. PDF metadata/page counts otherwise look as expected.\",\"ct\":1777302536.721409},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"## A. Verification pass\\n\\nMost v3 blockers landed, but **not all**. The remaining issues are consistency-level, not new scientific-review objections.\\n\\n### Landed\\n\\n**DNB**\\n- Title updated correctly.\\n- Table 4 **G=8** row now reads **81.2% / 34.4%**.\\n- Table 4 includes **G=32†**.\\n- Stratified paragraph landed: **r = +0.40, N=19** and **r = +0.13, N=7**.\\n- Pooled-correlation caption now explicitly says the pooled scatter is **task-confounded**.\\n- Bitter Lesson and model-varying Tier-B† rows are present in the manifest with step counts.\\n\\n**Workshop**\\n- “3B–671B” blocker is fixed; headline now uses **0.6B–671B total / 0.6B–37B active**.\\n- Qwen2.5-0.5B row is now **Modal L4**.\\n- Stratified GSM8K paragraph landed.\\n- No visible `Table ??`.\\n\\n**ZVF**\\n- Evidence-grade table demotes the stratified within-task result to **B**.\\n- “please cite these, not the pooled correlation” wording is gone.\\n- Closed-backend caveat is the cleanest of the three: it explicitly limits inferential claims to the mechanical theorem plus held-out 5-seed Qwen3-8B control.\\n- Title remains generic, as you said. The source TODO is not PDF-visible, so I cannot verify that from the PDFs alone.\\n\\n## Blockers / inconsistencies still present\\n\\n### 1. DNB seed accounting did **not** fully reconcile\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.6, Training Protocol** still says:\\n\\n> “the Tinker Qwen3-8B G-sweep is 3 seeds per cell across 14 cells”\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.6, Table 4 intro** still says:\\n\\n> “Tinker Qwen3-8B G-sweep at 3 seeds per cell”\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.7, Table 4 caption** still says:\\n\\n> “Tinker Qwen3-8B G-sweep rows have 3 seeds per cell”\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.26, checklist Q4** still says:\\n\\n> “+ 14 Tinker G-sweep rows + 4 Llama-3.3-70B-inst rows”\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.27, checklist Q7** still says:\\n\\n> “the 14 Tinker Qwen3-8B G-sweep rows”\\n\\nBut **main_dnb.pdf p.30 manifest** says:\\n\\n> `qwen3-8b (Wave-6 ablation) ... N=12 Seeds=1 Stepsmax=30`\\n\\nThat is a direct internal contradiction.\\n\\n### 2. G=32 is in main results/figures but absent from the manifest\\n\\nAcross the PDFs, the manifest group-size block lists only:\\n\\n> G=2, G=4, G=8, G=16\\n\\nBut **DNB Table 4 p.7** includes:\\n\\n> `Qwen3-8B (G=32)† ... Steps 11 ... 45.3% / 43.8%`\\n\\nAnd **DNB Figure 5 p.9**, **Workshop appendix p.16**, and **ZVF pp.7/21** all discuss or plot **G=32**.\\n\\nSo the “manifest reconciled cell-for-cell with main results” claim is still false unless G=32 is added to the manifest as partial/Tier-C or removed/clearly separated.\\n\\n### 3. Token-budget appendix still conflicts with the single-seed manifest\\n\\nAll three variants’ token-budget tables still say:\\n\\n> “3-seed mean”\\n\\nExamples:\\n- **main_dnb.pdf p.31, Table 9**\\n- **main_workshop.pdf p.16, Table 7**\\n- **main_zvf.pdf p.21, Table 5**\\n\\nBut the manifest now says the Wave-6 ablation is **N=12, Seeds=1**, and the group-size ablation rows are **single-seed per G**. If the token-budget reanalysis really uses separate 3-seed data, it needs a manifest row/source note. Otherwise change the captions and evidence grade.\\n\\nAlso, these token-budget tables include **G=64**, which is not present in the visible manifest.\\n\\n### 4. TBGU rename mostly landed, but one stale GU wording remains\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.9, Figure 5 caption** says:\\n\\n> “A token-budget-normalized reanalysis showing that the GU-optimal G shifts rightward…”\\n\\nGiven the rename, this should be **TBGU-optimal**, not GU-optimal.\\n\\n### 5. Closed-backend boilerplate alignment is incomplete in DNB/Workshop\\n\\n**ZVF** is aligned.\\n\\n**DNB** and **Workshop** still contain older/confusing language.\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.10** says:\\n\\n> “Train-set reward is the primary inferential signal in our held-out checks”\\n\\nThat sentence is internally confused and undermines the held-out-control framing.\\n\\n**main_workshop.pdf p.4** says:\\n\\n> “Train-set reward is the primary inferential signal in headline Tinker numbers”\\n\\nThis is exactly the phrasing I would avoid. It makes the train-set metric sound inferential rather than descriptive.\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.14** and **main_workshop.pdf p.8** still say primary statistical claims are drawn from open-source Modal/TRL runs. That is less clean than the ZVF version and does not match your stated cross-cutting fix: inferential claims limited to the mechanical theorem plus held-out 5-seed Qwen3-8B control, with Tinker stratified correlations as artifact analyses.\\n\\n### 6. Minor layout issue in DNB Table 4\\n\\n**main_dnb.pdf p.7**: the “Task 4 matched launcher comparison” subheading visibly overruns/clips at the right margin. Not a scientific blocker, but I would fix before E&D submission.\\n\\n## B. Readiness verdicts\\n\\n### DNB / E&D primary\\n\\n**Not ready as-is. Needs blocker fixes.**\\n\\nThe paper is otherwise in much better shape, but the DNB variant still has visible seed-accounting contradictions in the main text, table caption, checklist, and manifest. For an Evaluations & Datasets submission, that is exactly the kind of consistency issue reviewers will punish.\\n\\nRequired fixes:\\n1. Replace all stale “Qwen3-8B G-sweep, 3 seeds per cell, 14 cells” language with the Wave-6 / N=12 / 1-seed wording.\\n2. Add the G=32 partial row to the manifest, or remove G=32 from Table 4/Figure 5.\\n3. Resolve the “3-seed mean” token-budget captions and G=64 provenance.\\n4. Replace DNB closed-backend boilerplate with the cleaner ZVF-style wording.\\n5. Fix the Table 4 overrun.\\n\\nAfter those, I would treat DNB as the primary submission again.\\n\\n### Workshop\\n\\n**Close, but I would not upload as-is.**\\n\\nThe workshop variant fixed the major workshop-specific blockers, but it inherits the manifest/token-budget inconsistency and has the bad line:\\n\\n> “Train-set reward is the primary inferential signal in headline Tinker numbers”\\n\\nFor workshop, these are fast edits rather than deep blockers. Fix the wording and the manifest/token-budget provenance, then it is ready.\\n\\n### ZVF main\\n\\n**No change to the “do not submit to main track” verdict.**\\n\\nIt is substantially cleaner, especially the evidence-grade table and closed-backend caveat. But it remains a narrow, mostly negative, closed-backend/diagnostic audit with a generic title and still inherits the manifest/G=32/token-budget provenance inconsistency.\\n\\nUpdated estimate:\\n- **As-is:** ~10–15%.\\n- **After the small consistency fixes above:** ~15–20%.\\n- I still would not spend a main-track slot on it if DNB/E&D is available.\\n\\n## C. Anonymity sanity check\\n\\nNo hard deanonymizing residue found:\\n- No real author names in author blocks.\\n- No email addresses beyond the placeholder.\\n- PDF metadata Author fields are blank.\\n- No named collaborators; only “anonymous collaborator.”\\n- Canonical anonymous repo URL appears consistently: `anonymous.4open.science/r/agentic-grpo-bench-anon-2C6B`.\\n- GitHub URLs I saw are references/dataset/library citations, not author repo slugs.\\n\\nAmber, not red:\\n- Carbon sections still include regional hints:\\n  - **DNB p.12**, **Workshop p.6**, **ZVF p.11** mention **US-East**, **US average grid intensity**, **non-OECD national grids**, and a **0.4–0.8 kg CO2-eq/kWh** anonymized range.\\n  - **DNB p.15**, **Workshop p.9**, **ZVF p.14** say all authors are based at a single institution, with city/country withheld.\\n- Direct artifact slugs also appear outside the canonical anonymous URL in DNB: `wandb.ai/anonymous/tinker-rl-bench` and `huggingface.co/anonymous/tinker-rl-bench-*`. They are anonymous, but if the policy is “only canonical anonymous.4open.science,” route those through the anonymous repo instead.\\n\\nI would anonymize the carbon/location language further if aiming for strict double-blind: remove “non-OECD,” remove “US-East,” and say only “anonymized regional average.”\\n\\n## D. Updated submission strategy\\n\\nStrategy unchanged, but do a final patch before upload:\\n\\n1. **Primary:** DNB to NeurIPS 2026 E&D, after the seed/manifest/token-budget/closed-backend wording fixes.\\n2. **Workshop:** keep as workshop-ready fallback/parallel submission after the same small consistency patch.\\n3. **ZVF:** do not submit to main track; use as workshop/technical-report/appendix companion if needed.\\n\\nThe remaining issues are fixable, but I would not submit any of the three PDFs exactly as packaged.\",\"ct\":1777302939.774968}]},{\"id\":\"69ef6eee-5390-83e8-af24-965c1c443237\",\"title\":\"Round 3 Review ZVF\",\"create_time\":1777299183.173483,\"update_time\":1777300165.225085,\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"slug\":null,\"t\":\"Round 3 review. You previously reviewed v2 of three TinkerRL-Bench paper variants (main_zvf.pdf for NeurIPS main track, main_dnb.pdf for Evaluations & Datasets, main_workshop.pdf for a NeurIPS workshop) and gave 5/10 / 6/10 / 7/10. The author has applied your specific round-2 feedback and made one significant additional change: the ZVF main-track variant has been reframed so that the within-task null result is now the headline empirical contribution, not a caveat to a \\\"predictive diagnostic\\\" claim. Please review the v3 PDFs.\\n\\nWhat changed since v2 (with new contributions emphasized):\\n\\n1. ZVF main-track (main_zvf.pdf, 22pp):\\n   - **Reframed around the within-task null result.** New headline empirical claim: pooled cross-task ZVF-vs-performance correlation does NOT survive within-task stratification on GSM8K. Within-GSM8K Pearson r = +0.40 (p=0.09, N=19), restricted to model-varying GSM8K r = +0.13 (p=0.79, N=7). Pooled r=-0.769 (N=15) is now explicitly disclosed as task-identity-confounded and demoted to \\\"do not propagate\\\" in the evidence-grade table. Prescriptive recommendation: ZVF is per-step instrumentation inside a task, not a cross-task scoring statistic.\\n   - Section 4.2 restructured: stratified analysis is now under a \\\"Headline empirical result\\\" paragraph; pooled correlation is \\\"Auxiliary\\\".\\n   - Evidence-grade table now has a top tier \\\"Headline claims (please cite these, not the pooled correlation)\\\" with mechanical claim + within-task null as A-grade.\\n   - New ZVF-specific conclusion (conclusion_zvf.tex) that headlines the negative result and the narrow prescriptive recommendation.\\n   - Group-size: single-seed fixed-step winner is G=4 (last10=0.52, not G=8); main text + Appendix C reconciled. Token-budget reanalysis at T>=16M still favors G=32, framed as different budget axes.\\n   - Figure 1 (kl_proxy.pdf) regenerated: \\\"KL proxy\\\" / \\\"KL / update-magnitude proxies\\\" wording removed from the rendered figure itself.\\n   - Reproducibility: now distinguishes 3 release tiers explicitly (precomputed ZVF/GU traces; step-level aggregate logs; raw per-group rollout JSONL released for documented subset).\\n   - Stale \\\"Tinker 99.9% vs TRL 73.4%\\\" / \\\"verbosity-trap in 4/11 GRPO\\\" / \\\"Section 4.1 saturation analysis\\\" claims removed everywhere.\\n   - Parameter scale harmonized to \\\"0.6B-671B total (0.6B-37B active for largest MoE)\\\" everywhere.\\n   - Run manifest appendix added so cross-references resolve.\\n\\n2. Evaluations & Datasets (main_dnb.pdf, 30pp):\\n   - Section 4.1 / 5.2 / abstract / intro all harmonized to 0.6B-671B / 0.6B-37B active.\\n   - Figure 1 caption fixed: \\\"taxonomy of RL libraries\\\" -> \\\"taxonomy of tasks in TinkerRL-Bench\\\".\\n   - Carbon mismatch fixed: checklist no longer claims Modal sub-component is 0.4-1.2 kg; now points to Table 6 in ethics statement (5.1 kg).\\n   - Run manifest is now the source of truth; checklist Q4/Q5/Q7 reconciled against it (which Modal/TRL rows are 5-seed vs single-seed).\\n   - Reproducibility section: same 3-tier artifact framing as ZVF.\\n   - Tinker dagger marking commitment rewritten to be precise (italicized table headers + figure captions, not blanket dagger on every Tinker-only number).\\n\\n3. Workshop (main_workshop.pdf, 15pp):\\n   - Title softened: \\\"Exploratory Workshop Benchmark\\\" -> \\\"Exploratory Workshop Artifact\\\".\\n   - Group-size claim softened: removed \\\"G=8 sweet spot\\\", now \\\"non-monotonic; we do not headline a winning G\\\".\\n   - Reproducibility: same 3-tier release framing.\\n   - Stale \\\"99.9%\\\", \\\"4/11 verbosity\\\", \\\"Section 4.1 saturation\\\" leftovers removed from ethics_statement_anon.tex.\\n   - All other workshop content preserved; scientific content still ends well before page 8.\\n\\nWhat I want from you in this round:\\n\\nA. **NeurIPS-worthiness verdict for each variant.** Be specific: \\\"would I accept this at NeurIPS main / E&D / workshop if I were a reviewer assigned to it today?\\\" — yes / no / conditional. If no or conditional, the specific blocker.\\n\\nB. **For the ZVF main-track variant specifically:** is the reframing around the within-task null result strong enough to be a main-track contribution? If not, what specifically is missing? Is the within-task null result by itself a main-track-defensible scientific contribution, or does it need a positive companion claim? What would the strongest realistic version of this paper look like if no new experiments are possible?\\n\\nC. **Identify any new issues** the round-2/round-3 edits introduced — internal inconsistencies, broken cross-references, claims that no longer match the data, anonymity regressions.\\n\\nD. **Updated scores** out of 10 for each variant.\\n\\nE. **Updated submission strategy.** Should the author submit ZVF main-track at all, or stick with workshop primary + E&D fallback? If ZVF main-track is now plausible, what's the realistic acceptance probability?\\n\\nBe honest. The author would rather hear \\\"this is still not main-track\\\" than waste a submission slot. Conversely, if the within-task null reframing actually crossed the threshold, say so directly.\",\"ct\":1777299182.065},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc cat /home/oai/skills/pdfs/SKILL.md && echo '\\n---DOCX---' && cat /home/oai/skills/docx/SKILL.md | head -80\",\"ct\":1777299186.022279},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"I’ll review the actual v3 PDFs as a fresh pass, checking claim/data alignment, revised evidence framing, cross-references, appendices/checklists, anonymity, and regressions before giving verdicts and scores.\",\"ct\":1777299197.425223},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc cat /home/oai/skills/pdfs/tasks/read_review.md\",\"ct\":1777299202.891282},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"slug\":\"gpt-5-5-pro\",\"t\":\"bash -lc ls -l /mnt/data && unzip -l /mnt/data/neurips_review_v3.zip | sed -n '1,200p'\",\"ct\":1777299206.000235},{\"role\":\"assi